From 90e8cf1c9c398b8885060d386240fc68eb34b898 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenLogi contributor <contributor@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:12:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/19] feat(hidpp): decode and write stored G-series mouse
 profiles

Adds sector reads and writes (memoryAddrWrite / memoryWrite /
memoryWriteEnd) to OnboardProfilesFeature, and a pure codec for the
stored profile layout (formats 1-5, libratbag's internal profile):
report rate, DPI levels and shift, both LED zones with their
power-saving copies, and button bindings in both layers.

Editing is read-modify-write: only fields that differ from the
decoded original are re-encoded; every other byte (angle snapping,
power timeouts, the name) is copied through. A changed light keeps a
dimmed power-saving copy at its previous ratio, or half.

Also: CRC-16/CCITT sector checksums, switching a profile on in the
directory, and reading stored macros (format 1).

Fixtures are sectors from a G903 LIGHTSPEED HERO (format 4).
