From: OpenLogi contributor <contributor@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:50:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/19] feat(device): edit stored G-series profiles through a
 guarded write

Reads a mouse's user profiles whole (with the factory bindings and the
macros they point to), saves an edited profile, and selects a profile,
switching it on in the profile list first: the mouse refuses to select
a profile that is off (InvalidArgument on a G903 HERO).

Every write re-reads the sector until two reads agree, requires it to
still equal what the edit was based on and to carry a valid checksum,
hands the original to the caller's backup, writes, reads back and
compares; on a mismatch it writes the original back and checks that.
DPI levels are checked against the sensor's own list; without one, DPI
edits are refused.

Wire: WriteError::{OnboardProfileRejected, OnboardMemoryChanged,
OnboardBackupFailed, OnboardWriteNotStored} and
HidppOperation::WriteOnboard appended; PROTOCOL_VERSION 47.
