From: OpenLogi contributor <contributor@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:47:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/19] feat(agent): read, save and select stored G-series
 profiles over IPC

Agent::{read_stored_profiles, save_stored_profile,
select_stored_profile} appended, carrying new wire types in
openlogi_core::hid::stored_profile (mirrors of the 0x8100 codec, which
core must not depend on; the device crate converts).

A save sends the sector bytes the editor read; the device layer decodes
that base itself rather than trusting a caller's copy, lays the edited
settings over it (button lists keep the base's length, the
power-saving lights always come from the base) and runs the guarded
write.

Before every write the agent saves the sector to
data_dir()/onboard-backups/<route>/, as a new file that is read back;
a failed backup stops the write.

Part of PROTOCOL_VERSION 47.
