From c5dc8aa1828b628be4cebf08e3bf249ef5aab37d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenLogi contributor <contributor@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:40:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/19] feat(desktop): edit stored bindings from the Buttons
 panel itself

Replaces the separate stored-profile panel. While a stored profile is in
control, the mouse picture shows that profile's bindings as actions
(G HUB's one-chord macros read as their shortcut: Ctrl+Tab is Next
Tab), the picker offers only what a profile can hold, and a picked
action is written into the mouse at once, like a pick applies at once
in host mode. A line under the inspector says how the write went.

Adds KeyCombo::new to openlogi-core for building a combo from a stored
HID usage.
