From e4d6c8d4344c3dfca6cd02af954945d73c1e2807 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenLogi contributor <contributor@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:28:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/19] feat: stored report rate, and switching stored profiles
 on and off

While a stored profile is in control, the Pointer tab's report rate shows
that profile's rate and a pick is written into it (it was locked).

The Onboard Memory card gets a row of switches, one per stored profile,
and Enable All: a guarded write of the profile list's on/off flags. The
profile in use can't be switched off, and one profile always stays on.
A profile switched on then appears among the In control choices.

Wire: Agent::set_stored_profiles_enabled appended (part of
PROTOCOL_VERSION 47, still unreleased).
