From ae359ecba1f6c5fbd95c1357828d2960cd287a07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenLogi contributor <contributor@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:21:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/19] feat(desktop): any RGB color, and a mouse's lighting in
 its stored profile

The Lighting tab gets a Custom Color picker beside the swatches (the
kit's ColorPicker): any color, applied like a swatch.

While a stored profile is in control, a lighting change is also written
into both of the profile's lights (brightness folded into the color: a
stored fixed color has none of its own), so the mouse keeps it without
OpenLogi. The tab shows the profile's lighting: the color as picked
when the mouse holds exactly that, else the stored color.
