From e90f9ac6c9a1a4d4ae32da28406c731b695ceeeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenLogi contributor <contributor@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:01:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/19] fix(desktop): stored mouse lighting only; read stored
 profiles once onboard is known

A lighting change on a mouse running a stored profile was also written
live. The live write takes the lights into software control: it
competed with the profile write (changes took seconds), and when
OpenLogi quit the mouse fell back to its default light rather than the
profile's. Such a change now goes only into the profile, and OpenLogi's
remembered color for the mouse is cleared so the agent stops applying
one.

The stored profiles were read when the device was selected, which can
be before the mouse is known to have onboard memory; that read was then
skipped for good, leaving the report rate locked until something else
read them. They are now also read when the onboard read arrives.
