Subject: [PATCH 16/19] feat: user-set levels for the low-battery notice

Settings > General gets "Warn at" and "Warn again after" under the
low-battery notifications switch (number fields, 20 % and 30 % by
default, OpenLogi's own levels until now). The agent's notice decides
"low" by the warning level and "charged again" by the re-arm level,
kept above the warning level; a device that reports no percentage keeps
its own low/critical level. The battery colours elsewhere are
unchanged.

Not wire format: the agent reads AppSettings from config.toml.
